/-!
# The enveloping algebra of a Lie group acts faithfully on smooth functions

Let `G` be a finite-dimensional real Lie group with Lie algebra `𝔤`, the left-invariant
derivations of `C^∞⟮I, G; ℝ⟯`. The action of the universal enveloping algebra `U(𝔤)` on smooth
functions (`TauCeti.envelopingAction`) is faithful
(`TauCeti.envelopingAction_injective`). Hence `U(𝔤)` is isomorphic to the algebra
of operators on `C^∞⟮I, G; ℝ⟯` generated by the left-invariant vector fields
(`TauCeti.envelopingAlgEquivAdjoin`), which commute with left translations.

## The derivative action

A left-invariant derivation `X` differentiates along the exponential lines it generates:
`(X f)(g)` is the derivative at `t = 0` of `t ↦ f (g * lieExp (t • X))`
(`LeftInvariantDerivation.hasDerivAt_apply_mul_lieExp_smul`, in
`TauCeti.Geometry.Lie.Exponential.Derivative.Basic`). Iterating,
`Xⁿ ∈ U(𝔤)` acts by the `n`-th derivative along the same line
(`LeftInvariantDerivation.iteratedDeriv_apply_mul_lieExp_smul`).

## Faithfulness

For a linear form `ℓ` on `𝔤`, cut off `exp ∘ ℓ ∘ log` near the identity to a smooth function `f`
with `f (lieExp Y) = exp (ℓ Y)` for small `Y`
(`TauCeti.exists_contMDiffMap_eventually_apply_lieExp_eq`, in
`TauCeti.Geometry.Lie.Exponential.LocalInverse`). Along a line,
`t ↦ f (lieExp (t • X))` is `t ↦ exp (t ℓ X)` near `0`, so `Xⁿ` acts on `f` at the identity by
`(ℓ X)ⁿ`. The `n`-th powers span the degree-`n` symmetric tensors, so the symmetrization of a
homogeneous polynomial `p ∈ Sⁿ(𝔤)` acts on `f` at the identity by the value of `p` at `ℓ`. Every
element of `U(𝔤)` is a sum of symmetrizations
(`TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.iSup_range_pbwSymmetrization_eq_top`); if it acts by zero,
the corresponding polynomial vanishes at every linear form, so it is zero.

## Main results

* `LeftInvariantDerivation.iteratedDeriv_apply_mul_lieExp_smul`: `Xⁿ` is the `n`-th derivative
  along the exponential lines of `X`.
* `TauCeti.envelopingAction_injective`: **`U(𝔤)` acts faithfully on
  `C^∞⟮I, G; ℝ⟯`.**
* `TauCeti.envelopingAlgEquivAdjoin`: `U(𝔤)` is isomorphic to the algebra of
  operators generated by the left-invariant vector fields.

## References

* S. Helgason, *Differential Geometry, Lie Groups, and Symmetric Spaces*, Chapter II, §4,
  Theorem 4.3.
* F. W. Warner, *Foundations of Differentiable Manifolds and Lie Groups*, Exercise 3.22.
-/

public section

